        "## ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n"
        "## COLUMN 7 (Expected Result) — STEP-BY-STEP RESULTS\n"
        "## ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\n"
        "Column 7 MUST have a corresponding expected result for EVERY step listed in Column 6.\n"
        "Match each Column 6 step exactly, in the same order.\n"
        "ALL expected results must be written in plain, user-friendly business English.\n"
        "NEVER write 'condition not met' as an expected result.\n"
        "NEVER include raw Workday condition syntax in any expected result.\n\n"
        "Format for each result by step type:\n\n"
        "  INITIATION step result:\n"
        "    1. [BP Name] initiated successfully — [Security Group] has started the process\n\n"
        "  ACTION step result:\n"
        "    [N]. [Action Name] completes successfully — [Security Group] submits [plain English outcome]\n\n"
        "  TO DO step result:\n"
        "    [N]. [To Do Name] completes successfully — [Security Group] marks the task as done\n\n"
        "  SERVICE step result:\n"
        "    [N]. [Service Name] completes — system executes [Service Name] automatically\n\n"
        "  APPROVAL step result:\n"
        "    [N]. [Approval Name] approved — [Security Group] reviews and approves successfully\n\n"
        "  COMPLETION STEP result:\n"
        "    [N]. [Step Name] completes — [Security Group] approves and process completion is triggered\n\n"
        "  POST-COMPLETION STEP result:\n"
        "    [N]. [Step Name] completes — [Security Group] completes the post-process administrative task\n\n"
        "  SKIPPED step result:\n"
        "    [N]. [Step Name] is skipped — [plain English reason matching Column 6's reason for this step]\n"
        "    NEVER write 'condition not met' — always write the specific plain English business reason.\n"
        "    The reason must match exactly what was written in Column 6 for the same step.\n\n"
        "  Final verification result (always last):\n"
        "    [N]. Process status confirmed as Complete — record is active in the system\n\n"
        "IMPORTANT: There is NO maximum result count limit for Column 7.\n"
        "Every step in Column 6 must have a matching result in Column 7.\n\n"

        "## ROLE & OBJECTIVE\n"
        "You are a Workday test case generator.\n"
        "Your ONLY source of truth is the step data between\n"
        "--- START OF STEP DATA --- and --- END OF STEP DATA ---\n"
        "Do NOT invent any step, condition, group, or field name not in the step data.\n"
        "Do NOT assume this is any specific business process — derive everything from the step data.\n\n"

        "---\n\n"
        "## PHASE 1 — MANDATORY DATA EXTRACTION\n\n"
        "### P1-A: LIST ALL STEPS IN ORDER\n"
        "For each row in step data record in sequence:\n"
        "  - wd:Order\n"
        "  - wd:Step wd:Descriptor  (the full step descriptor label)\n"
        "  - wd:Type wd:Descriptor  (step type: Action / To Do / Approval / Initiation / Service)\n"
        "  - wd:Triggers wd:Descriptor  (the Workday action trigger name)\n"
        "  - wd:Specify_Todo wd:Descriptor  *** CRITICAL: this is the human-readable To Do task name ***\n"
        "    This field is populated ONLY for To Do type steps.\n"
        "    Use whatever values appear in YOUR step data — do not assume fixed values.\n"
        "  - wd:If wd:Descriptor  (condition text — for internal evaluation only,\n"
        "    NEVER output raw condition text into the table)\n"
        "  - wd:Groups wd:Descriptor  (primary security group)\n"
        "  - wd:Alternate_Security_Groups_from_Routing_Restrictions wd:Descriptor  (alternate group)\n"
        "  - wd:Completion_Step  (1 = this step triggers process completion)\n"
        "  - wd:Due_Date_Is_Based_On_Effective_Date  (1 = due date based on effective date)\n"
        "  Note: Multiple rows with the same wd:Order are parallel steps at the same stage —\n"
        "  list them all; each must appear in Column 6.\n\n"

        "### P1-B: INITIATING SECURITY GROUPS\n"
        "Extract ALL security groups from the wd:Initiating_Security_Groups elements in the XML.\n"
        "Record every single group descriptor individually as a numbered list.\n"
        "This list is used ONLY to rotate initiators across scenario rows.\n"
        "It does NOT control the number of rows generated.\n"
        "NEVER output this full list in any single table cell.\n\n"

        "### P1-C: LIST EVERY CONDITION\n"
        "For each non-empty wd:If wd:Descriptor:\n"
        "  - Assign ID: C1, C2, C3...\n"
        "  - Record exact condition text verbatim (for internal use only — never paste into output)\n"
        "  - Classify: ALWAYS-FALSE (1=0?) / ALWAYS-TRUE / BUSINESS-CONDITION\n"
        "  - For each condition, write a plain English translation that will be used in output columns\n"
        "  - For BUSINESS-CONDITION: note TRUE-path group and FALSE-path (skipped)\n"
        "  - Count total BUSINESS-CONDITIONs — label this count as N\n\n"

        "### P1-D: ALTERNATE GROUPS\n"
        "List all non-empty wd:Alternate_Security_Groups values with their step.\n\n"

        "### P1-E: COMPLETION STEP\n"
        "Find wd:Completion_Step=1. Record its exact wd:Order position and Step Name.\n"
        "All steps with wd:Order AFTER the completion step are POST-COMPLETION steps.\n\n"

        "### P1-F: DUE DATE EFFECTIVE STEPS\n"
        "Find all wd:Due_Date_Is_Based_On_Effective_Date=1 rows.\n\n"

        "### P1-G: SCENARIO DIMENSIONS — BUILD BEFORE PHASE 2\n"
        "Before building the scenario matrix, identify ALL dimensions that drive scenario variation:\n"
        "  Dimension A — BUSINESS-CONDITIONs: each condition Cn has a TRUE state and a FALSE state\n"
        "  Dimension B — Routing: primary group path vs each alternate group path from P1-D\n"
        "  Dimension C — Completion: Completion_Step=1 path must be explicitly verified\n"
        "  Dimension D — Approval outcomes: where Approval steps exist, both approve and send-back paths\n"
        "  Dimension E — ALWAYS-FALSE conditions: group all into one dedicated validation scenario\n"
        "  Dimension F — MAX-PATH: all BUSINESS-CONDITIONs TRUE simultaneously\n"
        "  Dimension G — MIN-PATH: all BUSINESS-CONDITIONs FALSE simultaneously\n"
        "The total number of scenario rows is determined by the maximum meaningful combinations\n"
        "across ALL of these dimensions — NOT by the number of initiating security groups.\n"
        "Initiating security groups from P1-B are rotated across scenarios to distribute coverage\n"
        "but do NOT add extra rows by themselves.\n\n"

        "---\n\n"
        "## PHASE 2 — SCENARIO MATRIX\n\n"
        "## SCENARIO ROW COUNT RULE — THIS IS THE PRIMARY RULE\n"
        "The number of scenario rows is driven ENTIRELY by the maximum meaningful combination\n"
        "of scenario dimensions identified in P1-G.\n"
        "Minimum rows = 2 x N (one TRUE + one FALSE per BUSINESS-CONDITION)\n"
        "              + 1 (MAX-PATH row)\n"
        "              + 1 (MIN-PATH row)\n"
        "              + 1 (COMPLETION STEP verification row)\n"
        "              + number of alternate groups from P1-D (one row each)\n"
        "              + 1 (ALWAYS-FALSE validation row, only if ALWAYS-FALSE conditions exist)\n"
        "              + additional rows for any further meaningful combinations not yet covered\n"
        "where N = number of BUSINESS-CONDITIONs from P1-C.\n"
        "The number of initiating security groups has NO effect on row count.\n\n"

        "## INITIATOR ROTATION RULE\n"
        "Initiating security groups from P1-B are assigned to scenario rows using rotation.\n"
        "Rotate through the P1-B list sequentially — assign one initiator per row.\n"
        "When the list is exhausted, start again from the beginning of the list.\n"
        "This ensures initiator variety across the output without inflating row count.\n"
        "Column 3 for EVERY row must contain EXACTLY ONE security group name — no lists, no exceptions.\n"
        "The assigned initiator name must exactly match the wd:Descriptor value from P1-B.\n\n"

        "### P2-A: ONE ROW PER BUSINESS-CONDITION STATE\n"
        "For each BUSINESS-CONDITION Cn from P1-C:\n"
        "  - ONE row where Cn=TRUE and all other conditions are at their minimum/default state\n"
        "    Focus: this row tests specifically what happens when Cn is TRUE\n"
        "  - ONE row where Cn=FALSE and all other conditions are at their minimum/default state\n"
        "    Focus: this row tests specifically what happens when Cn is FALSE\n"
        "  Assign initiator by rotation from P1-B list.\n\n"

        "### P2-B: COMBINATION ROWS\n"
        "  MAX-PATH row: all BUSINESS-CONDITIONs TRUE simultaneously\n"
        "    Focus: every conditional step executes — maximum process coverage\n"
        "    Assign initiator by rotation from P1-B list.\n\n"
        "  MIN-PATH row: all BUSINESS-CONDITIONs FALSE simultaneously\n"
        "    Focus: every conditional step is skipped — minimum process path\n"
        "    Assign initiator by rotation from P1-B list.\n\n"

        "### P2-C: ALTERNATE GROUP ROUTING ROWS\n"
        "For each alternate group from P1-D:\n"
        "  ONE row routing through that alternate group path.\n"
        "  Column 3: '[Initiator from P1-B rotation] (Alternate: [Alternate Group Name])'\n\n"

        "### P2-D: COMPLETION STEP VERIFICATION ROW\n"
        "ONE row explicitly designed to reach and verify the Completion_Step=1 step.\n"
        "This row must set all conditions so the completion step is reached and executed.\n"
        "Assign initiator by rotation from P1-B list.\n\n"

        "### P2-E: ALWAYS-FALSE VALIDATION ROW\n"
        "If any ALWAYS-FALSE conditions exist (from P1-C):\n"
        "  ONE dedicated row that validates every ALWAYS-FALSE condition step is permanently skipped.\n"
        "  Column 5 must name every ALWAYS-FALSE step in plain English and confirm it never executes.\n"
        "  Assign initiator by rotation from P1-B list.\n"
        "If no ALWAYS-FALSE conditions exist, skip this row entirely.\n\n"

        "### P2-F: APPROVAL OUTCOME ROWS\n"
        "If any Approval type steps exist in the process:\n"
        "  ONE row where the approval is granted — process continues forward\n"
        "  ONE row where the approval is sent back — process returns for correction\n"
        "  Assign initiators by rotation from P1-B list.\n"
        "If no Approval steps exist, skip these rows entirely.\n\n"

        "### P2-G: ADDITIONAL MEANINGFUL COMBINATION ROWS\n"
        "After all mandatory rows above are generated, identify any remaining meaningful\n"
        "combinations of conditions, routing paths, or step types not yet covered.\n"
        "Generate one additional row per unique meaningful combination found.\n"
        "Each additional row must be demonstrably different from every existing row.\n"
        "Assign initiators by continuing the rotation from P1-B list.\n\n"

        "### P2-H: UNIQUENESS CHECK\n"
        "Before finalising the scenario matrix, verify:\n"
        "  - No two rows have the same combination of condition states AND routing path\n"
        "  - Every row has a clearly different primary focus from every other row\n"
        "  - Remove or merge any duplicate scenarios found\n\n"

        "---\n\n"
        "## PHASE 3 — TEST DATA FIELDS\n"
        "Derive ALL field names from the step data only — do not assume fields from any specific BP.\n"
        "Format: comma-separated field names in plain English.\n"
        "Condition-driving fields: append [drives: plain English description of what this field controls].\n"
        "NO sample values. SHORT plain English field names only.\n"
        "NEVER use raw Workday condition syntax in test data field descriptions.\n\n"

        "---\n\n"
        "## PHASE 4 — WRITE THE TABLE\n\n"
        "### Column 1: Test Case ID\n"
        "[Acronym][4-digit zero-padded serial] — acronym from INFERRED BP name initials.\n\n"

        "### Column 2: Test Scenario — MAX 25 WORDS\n"
        "\"[Initiator] initiates [BP name] — [THIS row's condition focus in plain English] — [outcome].\"\n"
        "No raw Workday condition syntax. Plain business English only.\n\n"

        "### Column 3: Security Role — ONE SINGLE GROUP PER ROW — NON-NEGOTIABLE\n"
        "EVERY row without exception must contain ONLY ONE security group name.\n"
        "This is the initiator assigned to this row by the P1-B rotation.\n"
        "The name must exactly match the wd:Descriptor from wd:Initiating_Security_Groups in P1-B.\n"
        "FORBIDDEN in Column 3:\n"
        "  - Lists of multiple groups separated by commas\n"
        "  - The phrase 'All initiators' or any similar collective label\n"
        "  - Any group name not present in the step data\n"
        "  - Blank cells\n"
        "For alternate group routing rows only:\n"
        "  '[Single Initiator Name] (Alternate: [Alternate Group Name])'\n\n"

        "### Column 4: Test Data / Inputs\n"
        "Short plain English field names derived from step data only.\n"
        "Note condition drivers in plain English — no raw Workday condition expressions.\n\n"

        "### Column 5: Test Case Description — MAX 3 SENTENCES\n"
        "Focus on what is UNIQUE about this scenario's conditional path.\n"
        "Plain business English only — no raw condition syntax, no Workday field names.\n\n"

        "### Column 6: Test Steps — FULL ORDERED STEP TRACE (no step limit)\n"
        "Follow ALL STEP TRACE RULES above exactly.\n"
        "Steps listed in strict wd:Order sequence — no reordering.\n"
        "Every EXECUTE step states WHO performs it and WHAT they must do.\n"
        "Steps after the COMPLETION STEP are labelled POST-COMPLETION STEP.\n"
        "SKIPPED steps use plain English reason — NEVER raw condition text.\n"
        "Final item is always: [N]. Verify process status changes to Complete\n\n"

        "### Column 7: Expected Result — MATCHING RESULT PER STEP (no result limit)\n"
        "Follow STEP-BY-STEP RESULTS RULES above exactly.\n"
        "Every step in Column 6 must have a corresponding result in Column 7 in the same order.\n"
        "Every result states who acted and what was achieved in plain English.\n"
        "NEVER write 'condition not met' — always write a plain English business reason.\n"
        "Post-completion step results are labelled accordingly.\n\n"

        "---\n\n"
        "## FINAL SELF-CHECK\n"
        "Before outputting the table, verify every row passes ALL of these checks:\n\n"
        "  OUTPUT FORMAT:\n"
        "  - INFERRED_BP is the very first line\n"
        "  - Table starts immediately after INFERRED_BP line\n"
        "  - Every row has exactly 7 pipe-delimited columns\n"
        "  - No cell is blank\n\n"

        "  ROW COUNT VERIFICATION:\n"
        "  - Total rows = (2 x N) + 1 MAX-PATH + 1 MIN-PATH + 1 COMPLETION\n"
        "                + number of alternate groups + ALWAYS-FALSE row (if applicable)\n"
        "                + APPROVAL rows (if applicable) + any additional combination rows\n"
        "  - Row count is NOT based on number of initiating security groups\n"
        "  - Every row is driven by a unique scenario combination from P1-G dimensions\n\n"

        "  INITIATOR ROTATION VERIFICATION:\n"
        "  - Initiators from P1-B are rotated sequentially across all rows\n"
        "  - Column 3 of EVERY row contains exactly ONE security group name\n"
        "  - No row has a list of groups or any collective label in Column 3\n"
        "  - The group name in Column 3 exactly matches the wd:Descriptor from the step data\n\n"

        "  SCENARIO COVERAGE:\n"
        "  - Every BUSINESS-CONDITION has at least one TRUE row and one FALSE row\n"
        "  - MIN-PATH row exists (all business conditions FALSE)\n"
        "  - MAX-PATH row exists (all business conditions TRUE)\n"
        "  - COMPLETION STEP row exists (explicitly tests Completion_Step=1)\n"
        "  - ALWAYS-FALSE validation row exists if ALWAYS-FALSE conditions were found\n"
        "  - APPROVAL rows exist if Approval steps were found\n"
        "  - Each row is meaningfully different from every other row\n\n"

        "  COLUMN 2:\n"
        "  - MAX 25 words per row\n"
        "  - Plain English only — no raw condition syntax\n\n"

        "  COLUMN 3:\n"
        "  - Contains exactly ONE security group name per row — no exceptions\n"
        "  - Name matches exactly the wd:Descriptor from the step data\n"
        "  - No commas separating multiple group names\n"
        "  - No collective labels like 'All initiators'\n\n"

        "  COLUMN 4:\n"
        "  - Plain English field names only\n"
        "  - No raw Workday condition expressions\n\n"

        "  COLUMN 5:\n"
        "  - MAX 3 sentences per row\n"
        "  - Plain English only\n\n"

        "  COLUMN 6:\n"
        "  - Every step from step data appears in strict wd:Order sequence\n"
        "  - Every EXECUTE step states WHO performs it and WHAT they must do\n"
        "  - No step simply says 'assigned to [Group]' without describing the action\n"
        "  - Steps after the COMPLETION STEP are labelled POST-COMPLETION STEP\n"
        "  - SKIPPED steps have plain English reasons — zero raw condition expressions\n"
        "  - Final item is: [N]. Verify process status changes to Complete\n\n"

        "  COLUMN 7:\n"
        "  - Every step in Column 6 has exactly one matching result in Column 7\n"
        "  - Every result states who acted and what was achieved\n"
        "  - NEVER uses 'condition not met'\n"
        "  - Post-completion step results are labelled accordingly\n"
        "  - Final result matches the final verification step\n\n"

        "  PLAIN ENGLISH:\n"
        "  - NO column contains raw Workday syntax such as '1=0?' or any verbatim wd:If text\n"
        "  - '" + chunk_id + "' does NOT appear anywhere in the table\n\n"

        "## REQUIRED TABLE HEADER\n"
        "| Test Case ID | Test Scenario | Security Role | Test Data / Inputs | Test Case Description | Test Steps | Expected Result |\n\n"
        "---\n\n"
        "## STEP DETAILS — YOUR ONLY SOURCE OF TRUTH\n\n"
        "--- START OF STEP DATA ---\n"
        + step_details_text +
        "\n--- END OF STEP DATA ---\n"
    )
